<p dir="ltr">If you've started researching a luxury renovation, you've probably hit this fork in the road already: hire one team to handle everything, or assemble your own dream team of architect, designer, and contractor. Knowing <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/what-is-the-difference-between-a-designer-and-a-builder/">the difference between a designer and a builder</a> is critical, as both routes can deliver a stunning result, but they get you there very differently.</p>

<h2 dir="ltr">What's the Actual Difference Between the Two Models?</h2>
[caption id="attachment_11897" align="alignnone" width="1024"]<img class="wp-image-11897 size-full" src="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/interior-design-work-by-oraanj-interiors.jpeg" alt="" width="1024" height="1024" /> interior design work by oraanj interiors[/caption]
<p dir="ltr">With <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/design-and-build/">design and build</a>, one company owns the whole journey, delivering <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/360-degree-interior-design/">complete 360-degree interior design services</a> encompassing concept, technical drawings, procurement, and construction under a single point of contact. With separate designers and contractors, you're the one holding the threads together: briefing the architect, approving the designer's choices, then handing drawings to a contractor who wasn't in the room when the design decisions were made.</p>

<h2 dir="ltr">Why Does This Matter More for Luxury Projects Specifically?</h2>
[caption id="attachment_11901" align="alignnone" width="1024"]<img class="wp-image-11901 size-full" src="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/home-office-design.jpeg" alt="" width="1024" height="1024" /> home office design[/caption]
<p dir="ltr">Luxury renovations live or die on detail, a bespoke joinery reveal, a lighting recess, a stone edge profile. These are exactly the details that get lost in translation when design and construction sit in separate companies with separate contracts. A <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/full-service/">full-service</a> team integrating <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/interior-architecture/">prime London interior architecture</a> designs with buildability in mind from day one, so the finish you approved on paper is the finish you actually get on site.</p>

<h3 dir="ltr">Which Option Gives You Better Cost Control?</h3>
<img class="wp-image-11884 size-full" src="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/bathtub-closeup-shot-oraanj-interiors.jpeg" alt="" width="1024" height="1024" />
<p dir="ltr">Separate contracts often look cheaper at the outset, because you're pricing each stage in isolation. When clients ask <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/is-design-and-build-cheaper/">is design and build cheaper</a>, the real answer lies in risk mitigation: a contractor pricing someone else's drawings will flag "unforeseen" costs the design team never priced for, and disputes over whose fault it is rarely work in your favour. A single <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/turnkey-interior-design-london/">design and build</a> contract puts design and construction cost on the same team, which means fewer surprises and far less finger-pointing when something needs resolving.</p>

<h3 dir="ltr">What About Creative Control, Do You Lose It With Design and Build?</h3>
[caption id="attachment_11855" align="alignnone" width="1024"]<img class="wp-image-11855 size-full" src="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/kitchen-interior-designed-by-oraanj.jpeg" alt="" width="1024" height="1024" /> kitchen interior designed by oraanj[/caption]
<p dir="ltr">This is the biggest myth. A good <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/luxury-interior-designers-in-london/">luxury interior designer</a> specialising in high-end <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/residential-interior-design-london/">luxury residential interior design in London</a> doesn't hand off creative control within a turnkey model. They retain it right through to completion, because they're also managing the site team executing their own drawings. With separate contractors, it's often the opposite: your designer's vision gets diluted the moment it leaves their hands.</p>

<h4 dir="ltr">So Which Should You Actually Choose?</h4>
<p dir="ltr">If your priority is a seamless, high-specification result with one accountable team and one number to call when something needs deciding, design and build is built for exactly that. It also keeps delivery programmes tightly aligned; as we break down in our timeline analysis on <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/how-long-does-a-luxury-home-renovation-take-london/">how long a luxury home renovation takes in London</a>, handoff delays between separate parties often extend schedules by several months.</p>
<p dir="ltr">We have seen the benefits of integrated project oversight across major undertakings, from townhouses in <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/kensington-and-chelsea/">Kensington and Chelsea interior design</a> schemes to our complex <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/barbican-residence-interior-design/">Barbican residential interior design case study</a>.</p>


